From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: 993 - do not take a zero client count from a HAL that has the clients

The controller was told a node had no clients while two were associated to
it, and one of them was the machine asking the question.

The count comes straight from the BSS status reply:

	if (tb[8])
		ap->num_sta = blobmsg_get_u32(tb[8]);

and the HAL answers that field with 0 while its own assoclist, on the very
same ubus object, returns the clients. Measured 2026-08-26 on an agent
serving two:

	iw dev ap-mld-1 station dump      2 stations
	ubus wifi.ap.ap-mld-1 assoclist   both clients returned
	ubus wifi.ap.ap-mld-1 status      "num_stations": 0

The assignment is unconditional, so it also overwrites what the agent had
already counted for itself in wifi_add_sta(). From there the damage is quiet
and complete. The Associated Clients TLV is laid out as

	bssid | num_sta | num_sta * (macaddr | conntime)

so a zeroed num_sta emits an entry with no clients in it, even though
ap->stalist is holding them - the station list in `map.agent status` shows
the clients while num_sta beside it reads 0. The controller stores nothing,
its database reports nobody, and the overview shows zero clients on a mesh
that is serving them. Restarting the agent does not help: the next status
reply zeroes it again.

Believe the HAL when it reports clients, and keep our own count when it
reports none while we are still holding some. A genuine last-client-leaves
empties stalist as well, so a real zero is still recorded.

This is a workaround at the reader. status and assoclist disagreeing inside
one HAL object is a libwifi defect and belongs fixed there; until it is, the
agent should at least not repeat it.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/agent.c
+++ b/src/agent.c
@@ -3709,8 +3709,34 @@
 	if (tb[9])
 		ap->enabled = blobmsg_get_bool(tb[9]);
 
-	if (tb[8])
-		ap->num_sta = blobmsg_get_u32(tb[8]);
+	if (tb[8]) {
+		uint32_t hal_num_sta = blobmsg_get_u32(tb[8]);
+
+		/* 993: the HAL reports 0 here while its own assoclist on the
+		 * same object returns the clients (measured 2026-08-26). This
+		 * assignment is what reaches the Associated Clients TLV, whose
+		 * layout is bssid|num_sta|num_sta*(macaddr|conntime) - so a
+		 * zero emits an entry with no clients while ap->stalist holds
+		 * them, and the controller is told the node is empty. Believe
+		 * a non-zero count. When the HAL says none but we are still
+		 * holding stations, count them ourselves - keeping the previous
+		 * value is not enough: it goes stale the moment a second client
+		 * joins, and the TLV then reports one while two are associated
+		 * (measured 2026-08-26 evening, radio 2 / num_sta 1). A real
+		 * last-client-leaves empties stalist too, so a genuine zero
+		 * still lands. */
+		if (hal_num_sta > 0 || list_empty(&ap->stalist)) {
+			ap->num_sta = hal_num_sta;
+		} else {
+			struct sta *s;
+			uint32_t n = 0;
+
+			list_for_each_entry(s, &ap->stalist, list)
+				n++;
+
+			ap->num_sta = n;
+		}
+	}
 
 
 	if (!ap->enabled && agent_may_enable_fhs(ap->agent))
